===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|spiegel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|spiegal}} or {{m|goh|spēgal}}, from {{der|de|ML.|speglum}}, from {{der|de|la|speculum}}.
Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|Spegel}}, {{cog|nl|spiegel}}<ref>{{R:EWddS|ed=22|hw=Spiegel}}</ref>, {{cog|hrx|Spieghel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃpiːɡ(ə)l/}}
* {{a|Germany}} {{audio|de|De-Spiegel.ogg}}
* {{a|Austria}} {{audio|de|De-at-Spiegel.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Spiegels|Spiegel|Spiegelchen|dim2=Spieglein}}

# [[mirror]] {{gloss|smooth surface, usually made of glass with reflective material painted on the underside, that reflects light}}
#* {{quote-book|de|year=1812|author={{w|Brüder Grimm|lang=de}}|title=Schneewittchen|url={{fullurl:s:de:Sneewittchen_(Schneeweißchen)_(1812)}}|passage={{...}} Sie hatte auch einen '''Spiegel''', vor den trat sie alle Morgen und fragte: / „'''Spieglein''', '''Spieglein''' an der Wand: / wer ist die schönste Frau in dem ganzen Land?“|translation=She had a '''Mirror''' before which she came every morning. She'd ask: '''Mirror''', '''Mirror''', on the wall, who is the fairest Woman in the entire land?"}}
#: {{ux|de|Sie hatte einen großen '''Spiegel'''.|She had a large '''mirror'''.|inline=1}}
# [[level]] (of a liquid)
#: {{syn|de|Pegel|Konzentration}}
#: {{ux|de|Meeres'''spiegel'''|sea '''level'''|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|Alkoholspiegel|alcohol '''level''' (amount in blood, for example)|inline=1}}
# [[surface]] {{gloss|flat overside or up-side of a liquid}}
#: {{syn|de|Wasseroberfläche}}
# schematic [[overview]], [[table]] {{gloss|two-dimensional presentation of data}}
#: {{syn|de|Tabelle}}
#: {{ux|de|Noten'''spiegel'''|transcript (as in a set of notes that '''mirrors''' the conversation)|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|de|Gehalts'''spiegel'''|salary tables (pay '''levels''')|inline=1}}
# [[white]] or [[light]]-coloured [[mark]] (on an animal)
## {{n-g|on the forehead of [[horse]]s and [[cattle]]}}
##: {{ux|de|Das Pony hatte einen hübsch geformten '''Spiegel''' auf der Stirn.|The pony had a nicely shaped '''mark''' on the forehead.}}
## {{n-g|on the wing of a [[goose]], [[capercaillie]], or [[black cock]]}}
## {{n-g|on the [[hindquarters]] of [[deer]]}}

